ducation. So good decision, calm, technical, but communication and development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. So strong problem solving, responsibility, but temper and attitude.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some concerns. Which candidate balances? Candidate B handles stress well, conscientious, but nasty remarks is serious for crew cooperation. Candidate C calm, good decisions, but communication issues and egocentric, not good for crew. Candidate D problem solving, responsibility, but hot temper and know-it-all may affect crew. Candidate A leadership, anticipation, but show-off and not open to new ideas may affect adaptability.\n\nProbably Candidate B's stress handling and conscientiousness are crucial, but nasty remarks is big. Maybe D? Hot temper is serious. A's show-off maybe less severe? Not open to new ideas is concerning for adaptability. I'd lean towards Candidate C? Calm, correct decisions, technical, but communication issues are serious for crew cooperation. Hmm.\n\nWe need to make an initial recommendation. Could pick Candidate B as leading, but note concerns. Or we could say we need more info. But we must state a vote. Let's pick Candidate B as current recommendation, citing strengths: very conscientious, handles stress well, good weather assessment, but note concerns about nasty remarks. We'll argue that strengths outweigh concerns, but we need to address crew cooperation. We'll say we still recommend B but open to discussion.\n\nWe must not ask tool yet. Provide public message."}
